    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d22">

                <pb facs="0080" n="18" sameAs="frus:frus1878/pg18"/>

                <head>No. 17.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Evarts to Mr. Garcia</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1878-11-13"><hi rendition="#italic">November</hi> 13,
                        1878</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to inform you that the
                    President has taken into deliberate and mature consideration your note to this
                    Department of the 25th of March last, with the accompanying documents, books,
                    and maps, relative to the question submitted to his arbitrament by the
                    Governments of the Argentine Confederation and Paraguay, in regard to the
                    ownership of the territory on the west bank of the Paraguay, between the main
                    branch of the Pilcomayo and the Verde Rivers. The conclusion which he has
                    reached is embodied in the instrument<anchor n="*" xml:id="d22-f1"/> which I
                    have the honor to inclose, and decides the question in favor of Paraguay.</p>
                <p>I avail, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>WM. M. EVARTS.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d22-f1" n="*" xml:id="d22-f1-content">
                <p>For inclosure see note to Paraguayan minister, post.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
